{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0.01,"avg_sec":136.21,"success_pct":0.955},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] non-atomic-writes -- The supervisor writes to control/*.log files (supervisor.log, server.out.log, server.err.log, driver.*.log) using Out-File -Append. These writes are not atomic; a crash during write can produce partial lines or corrupt the log file. Multiple processes (supervisor + child processes) may write to the same log file concurrently, causing interleaved output. | Recommend: Use a logging function that writes to a dedicated log file per process with a mutex or use Windows EventLog for structured logging. Alternatively, use a single log file with a mutex (similar to Invoke-CircuitLogMutex in circuit-breaker.ps1).","commit":"b6f4e07752f2435e7ac375a0db52948c5bbcb117","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-05-30T09:50:36.7032140Z"}
