{"baseline":{"timeout_pct":0.01,"avg_sec":134.1,"success_pct":0.955},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] retry-loop-without-bounds -- The watchdog\u0027s main loop (while ($true)) has no bounded retry or exit condition. If the bridge root path ($b) becomes invalid or git.exe is missing, the watchdog will loop forever, logging errors every 2 minutes. This is a minor issue because the watchdog is designed to run indefinitely, but it could be improved with a fatal-exit after N consecutive critical errors. | Recommend: Add a consecutive-failure counter; after 10 consecutive critical errors (e.g., missing git.exe, cannot read auth.json), log a fatal message and exit the process to avoid silent log bloat.","commit":"f71938941c13cb40ab609c6dc9bce6b6875a533a","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-05-30T11:44:44.0251829Z"}
