unction correctly and analyze registry drift as intended.\r\n[[/PARALLEL:wp1]]\r\n\r\nITEM 2: backlog_id=bb308fc3f0aa451faa2a6a16c91bfe6d\r\nworkpack=wp-20260531101306-module-llm-54aee1; conflict_group=llm\r\nFiles: llm\r\nTask: [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] process_supervision -- Start-Srv and Start-Drv use Start-Process with -NoNewWindow but redirect stdout/stderr to files. If the log files are locked or the disk is full, the process may hang or fail silently. No retry logic or timeout is applied to the process start. | Recommend: Wrap Start-Process in a try/catch with a timeout. Verify the log file can be opened for writing before spawning. Add a fallback to write to a temp location if the primary log path fails.\r\n\r\n[[PARALLEL:wp2]]\r\nFiles: llm\r\nComplexity: moderate\r\nTask: [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] process_supervision -- Start-Srv and Start-Drv use Start-Process with -NoNewWindow but redirect stdout/stderr to files. If the log files are locked or the disk is full, the process may hang or fail silently. No retry logic or timeout is applied to the process start. | Recommend: Wrap Start-Process in a try/catch with a timeout. Verify the log file can be opened for writing before spawning. Add a fallback to write to a temp location if the primary log path fails.\r\n[[/PARALLEL:wp2]]\r\n\r\nITEM 3: backlog_id=dff0dce58f62498ea4f5650f3900606e\r\nworkpack=wp-20260531101306-module-memory-070e1f; conflict_group=memory\r\nFiles: memory\r\nTask: [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] process_supervision -- Reap-Bloated kills tracked processes with private memory \u003e 8GB. The 8GB threshold is hardcoded and may be too low for systems with large memory or for processes that legitimately use more memory during heavy operations. No warning or gradual escalation is performed before killing. | Recommend: Make the memory threshold configurable via config or environment variable. Add a warning log at 6GB and a grace period before killing. Consider using working set instead of private memory for the check.\r\n\r\n[[PARALLEL:wp3]]\r\nFiles: memory\r\nComplexity: moderate\r\nTask: [deep-agent/reliability-model/deepseek-v4-flash] process_supervision -- Reap-Bloated kills tracked processes with private memory \u003e 8GB. The 8GB threshold is hardcoded and may be too low for systems with large memory or for processes that legitimately use more memory during heavy operations. No warning or gradual escalation is performed before killing. | Recommend: Make the memory threshold configurable via config or environment variable. Add a warning log at 6GB and a grace period before killing. Consider using working set instead of private memory for the check.\r\n[[/PARALLEL:wp3]]\r\n\r\nSTATUS: CONTINUE","commit":"8d9fbe5860aa88e46bf0803839a369e567bc5322","type":"hypothesis","ts":"2026-05-31T08:03:06.1053739Z"}
