{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":11.98,"success_pct":0.02},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [project-autopilot server-connectivity-check-script] [[NORMAL]]\n\nCreate scripts/check-server.ts — HTTP connectivity check for running app\n\nWork in C:\\Users\\rafie\\bridge-projects\\private-community.\n\nCreate `scripts/check-server.ts` — a lightweight HTTP connectivity check that verifies a running Next.js server is responding correctly at key endpoints. This complements the manual smoke-checklist.md with a fast programmatic check.\n\nScript requirements:\n1. Accept optional env var `BASE_URL` (default: `http://localhost:3000`).\n2. Make HTTP GET requests to each of these endpoints and check expected status:\n   - `GET /login` → expect 200 (public page)\n   - `GET /register` → expect 200 (public page)\n   - `GET /feed` → expect 200 or 302 (redirect to login for unauthenticated is also acceptable)\n   - `GET /api/chat/messages` → expect 401 (unauthenticated API must reject)\n   - `GET /api/photos/upload` → expect 405 (no GET) or 401 (unauthenticated)\n3. For each check, print: PASS or FAIL, the endpoint, expected vs. actual status.\n4. Print a summary: \u0027✅ N/N checks passed\u0027 or \u0027❌ N/N checks passed — M failed\u0027.\n5. Exit 0 if all checks pass, exit 1 if any fail.\n6. If the server is not reachable at BASE_URL, print \u0027Server not reachable at \u003cBASE_URL\u003e\u0027 and exit 1.\n7. Use only Node.js built-ins (no axios/got/node-fetch): use `http`/`https` modules or `fetch` (Node 18+).\n\nAlso:\n- Add to `package.json` scripts: `\"check-server\": \"tsx scripts/check-server.ts\"`\n\nAcceptance:\n- `npm run typecheck` → exit 0\n- `npm run build` → exit 0\n- Running `npx tsx scripts/check-server.ts` when no server is running prints \u0027Server not reachable\u0027 and exits 1 (verifiable in sandbox without a running server)\n- Commit: \u0027feat: add HTTP server connectivity check script\u0027\n\nFiles: scripts/check-server.ts, package.json","after_tur