{"delta":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":11.7,"success_pct":0.02},"task":"[Автозадача из бэклога] [project-autopilot runbook-md-create] [[NORMAL]]\n\nCreate RUNBOOK.md operational guide for the operator\n\nWork in C:\\Users\\rafie\\bridge-projects\\private-community.\n\nCreate RUNBOOK.md — a practical operational guide for the person running the server. This is a new file.\n\nThe runbook must cover:\n\n## RUNBOOK.md structure:\n\n### 1. First-time setup (Day 1)\n- Clone repo and install: `npm install`\n- Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in SESSION_SECRET, ADMIN_LOGIN, ADMIN_SECRET\n- Generate session secret: `node -e \"console.log(require(\u0027crypto\u0027).randomBytes(32).toString(\u0027hex\u0027))\"`\n- Run `npm run pre-launch-check` — verify go/no-go before first launch\n- Run `npm run db:generate \u0026\u0026 npm run db:migrate`\n- Run `npm run seed:admin` to create admin account\n- Run `npm run build \u0026\u0026 npm run start` (or `npm run dev` for development)\n- Run `npm run setup-backup-task` to register daily backup in Windows Task Scheduler\n\n### 2. Starting and stopping the server\n- Dev: `npm run dev`\n- Production: `npm run build` then `npm run start`\n- Stop: Ctrl+C in the terminal running the server\n\n### 3. Daily monitoring\n- Check disk usage: `npm run check-storage` (warn if \u003e10 GB)\n- Verify connectivity: `npm run check-server` (requires running server)\n- Check backup dir: verify `backups/` has a recent entry (yesterday\u0027s timestamp)\n\n### 4. Manual backup\n- Run `scripts\\backup.ps1` (Windows) or `bash scripts/backup.sh`\n- Verify new directory created in `backups/backup-\u003ctimestamp\u003e/` with dev.db and storage/\n\n### 5. Restore from backup\n1. Stop the server\n2. Replace `prisma/dev.db` with the backup copy\n3. Replace `storage/` with the backup copy\n4. Start the server\n\n### 6. Adding a new admin\n- Set ADMIN_LOGIN and ADMIN_SECRET in .env\n- Run `npm run seed:admin`\n\n### 7. Common troubleshooting\n- Server won\u0027t start: run `npm run pre-launch-check` to identify the issue\n- SESSION_SECRET error: generate a new secret and set it in .env\n- Database missing: run `npm run db:migrate`\n- Storage not writable: check permissions on storage/ directory\n- Check disk space: `npm run check-storage`\n\n### 8. Quick command reference\nA table of all `npm run` commands with one-line descriptions (same as LAUNCH_READINESS.md operational scripts section, plus build/dev/start/db commands).\n\nAcceptance:\n- RUNBOOK.md is created with all 8 sections above\n- Commands are accurate and match what\u0027s actually in package.json\n- No secrets or sensitive data in the file\n- Docs-only: no typecheck/build required\n- Commit: \u0027docs: add RUNBOOK.md operational guide for operator\u0027\n\nFiles: RUNBOOK.md","after_turns":193,"after":{"timeout_pct":0,"avg_sec":120.39,"success_pct":1},"hypothesis_ts":"2026-06-02T01:56:30.1726621Z","type":"verdict","verdict":"no_effect","ts":"2026-06-03T23:00:09.7750932Z","commit":"83a038bf63633f4e980bbd3337858fefbfb7cb6f"}
